{
  "kanji": "滴",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 滴\ntitle: drip; drop\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 14\nradical: 水\nradicalNumber: 85\nonyomi: [テキ]\nkunyomi: [しずく, したた.る]\ndistractors: [商, 適, 高]\n---\n\n# 滴 — drip; drop\n\n**Strokes:** 14 · **Key (radical):** 水 (no. 85) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n滴 concerns drops of liquid and the action of dripping. A drop need not be water; 水滴 specifically identifies a water droplet.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Picture a drop falling beside the tall, enclosed-looking shape on the right, as though water were dripping from a narrow vessel.\n\nThe indexing radical 水 appears as 氵 at the left.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| テキ | on | [水滴](../words/水滴.md) すいてき - water droplet |\n| しずく | kun | 滴 しずく - drop; drip, a noun |\n| したた.る | kun | 滴る したたる - drip; trickle down |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [水滴](../words/水滴.md) すいてき - water droplet\n- 滴 しずく - drop of liquid\n\n## Notes\n\n- 滴 しずく is a noun; 滴る したたる is an intransitive godan verb: 滴って したたって.\n- 雫 is another spelling of しずく. It does not establish a different pronunciation for this card's noun.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1371880, 1437210, 1437230.\n",
